<p>-edit : Somebody fixed all the issues I complained about below! Huzzah!</p>
<p>&#8212;Alright, here's some useful feedback then:</p>
<p>The reason I was uncertain I had figured it out correctly was that I found it too implausible that nobody in any of the three anomalous groups at all showed any indication of suspecting where the light rail system was coming from. That is what broke my suspension of disbelief and made me suspect that I was interpreting things wrong, because it was too heavy on the idiot ball.</p>
<p>I suggest adding some kind of indirect indication that <em>somebody, anybody</em> in any of the three groups has even a teeny tiny little suspicion/hunch that either :</p>
<p>A: The park is making the rail system. Why wouldn't they suspect this if they have already observed the park making new habitats to fit animals that are introduced to the park? It's implausible that nobody has. (unless anti-memes? but that may be overkill)</p>
<p>B: One of those &quot;other two&quot; groups is trying to get away with installing the rail system on the down-low and won't fess up. I like this one better because it can add a sprinkle of tension between the three groups in their correspondence sections.&#8212;</p>

